							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "**Managed execution** ({{gtMethod:TestExecutionEnvironment>>#runExampleEvaluator:}}):\n- Signals the watchdog semaphore to start timing\n- Calls {{gtMethod:TestExecutionEnvironment>>#runExampleUnderWatchdogUsingEvaluator:}}\n- Will signal `TestTookTooMuchTime` if the example exceeds its time limit, {{gtMethod:GtExample>>#timeLimit}} (the {{gtPragma:timeLimit:}} pragma, by default {{gtMethod:GtExample>>#defaultTimeLimit}}, 1 minute)\n- Calls {{gtSymbol:handleCompletedTest}} on services when done\n- Calls {{gtSymbol:cleanUpAfterTest}} after every example: terminates forked processes, cancels unfinished promises and stops the thread pool of the example"
						},
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-05-27T10:59:43.089+02:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-12T22:54:00.087008-03:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "5HJNSLyUQUWbxUtBbIo1JA=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "**Unmanaged execution** ({{gtMethod:TestExecutionEnvironment>>#runUnmanagedExampleEvaluator:}}):\n- Sets the evaluator as the current `testCase` (for Epicea logging checks)\n- Executes the evaluator directly without watchdog timing\n- Disables the services that clean up after a test and does not clean up, so processes and promises the example starts keep running\n- If a test case or an example is already running, the evaluator simply runs as a part of it, so the running one's clean up still covers it"
						}
					]
				},
